==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*kweþaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*gʷet-}} (compare Proto-Celtic {{term/t|cel-pro|*bet-lo-||mouth}} in Old Irish {{term|bél|lang=sga}}). Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|qwetha|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon {{term|queþan|lang=osx}}, Old Dutch {{term|quethan|lang=odt}} (Middle Dutch {{term|quedden|lang=dum}}), Old High German {{term|quedan|lang=goh}}, Old Norse {{term|kveða|lang=non}} (Icelandic {{term|kveða|lang=is}}, Danish {{term|kvæde|lang=da}}, Swedish {{term|kväda|lang=sv}}), Gothic {{term|𐌵𐌹𐌸𐌰𐌽|tr=qiþan|sc=Goth|lang=got}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkweθɑn/|lang=ang}}

